# Local-only demo video production (Remotion project, captured data
# snapshots, voiceover recording, rendered output). Deliberately excluded
# by explicit user instruction -- never meant to reach the repo, unlike
# the *.md exceptions further down which are the opposite mistake
# (real docs wrongly caught by a blanket rule). Don't "fix" this one.
video/

# Reference/inspiration material the user dropped in the repo root for
# Claude to study (a Canva pitch-deck template), explicitly never meant to
# ship -- not the user's own work, no license to redistribute it.
Black Brown and White Gradient Modern Business Pitch Deck Presentation.pdf

venv/
.env
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
output/data/*.csv
!output/data/spread_backtest_results.csv
!output/data/evidence_gate_results.csv
!output/data/reconstruction_2016_2026.csv
!output/data/equity_curve.csv
output/audit/*.jsonl
.claude/

# Markdown is ignored by default, with the project documents allowed through.
# The research story is the differentiator, so these must be visible in the public repo.
*.md
!README.md
!EXPERIMENT.md
!OPTIONS_SYSTEM_PLAN.md
!VOLATILITY_ML_PLAN.md
!PROGRESS.md
!TRADING_SYSTEM_PLAN.md
!ML_Experiment_Plan.md
!RESEARCH_pooling_vs_individual.md
!EXPERIMENT_28_VRP.md
!EXPERIMENT_29_SHARPE_AUDIT.md
# SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md is internal multi-session coordination (who owns
# what, CI status pings), not research narrative -- deliberately excluded
# from the public repo even though the *.md blanket rule below would allow
# it back in. Already-tracked from an earlier commit, so removing it here
# also needs `git rm --cached` to actually stop tracking it.
# WRITEUP.md is the actual hackathon submission document -- caught silently
# by the same blanket *.md rule that already hid EXPERIMENT_28_VRP.md,
# SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md, and three reproducibility CSVs before it. Found
# during a final pre-submission stress test, same day as the deadline.
!WRITEUP.md
# Reproducibility fix (found during Experiment 29's own verifiability check):
# reconstruct.replay() -- and everything downstream of it (vrp_measure.py,
# pipeline/falsify/audit.py) -- needs these three to run at all. They were
# never committed, so a fresh clone cannot reproduce ANY of those, silently
# contradicting every "no network, no credentials" claim this project makes
# about them. Small (48-72KB), public market data, same category as the
# already-tracked vix.csv -- safe and consistent to commit.
!output/data/raw_SPY_long.csv
!output/data/vix9d.csv
!output/data/vix3m.csv
# Same blanket output/data/*.csv rule, caught proactively this time (W5,
# before it became a "found during a stress test" incident like the three
# above): pipeline/backtest/qqq_iwm_viability.py needs these to reproduce
# at all. Same category -- small, public daily-close market data.
!output/data/raw_QQQ_long.csv
!output/data/raw_IWM_long.csv
.vercel
.env*
# .env.example is a template with placeholder values only (no secrets --
# checked its contents before adding this) and scripts/security_preflight.py
# reads it to know which env var NAMES to scan for. The blanket .env* rule
# above caught it silently, same failure mode as raw_SPY_long.csv/vix9d.csv/
# vix3m.csv: a judge's fresh clone had no template to fill in, and
# security_preflight.py itself crashed with FileNotFoundError. .env and
# .env.local (real values) correctly stay ignored -- only the template is
# exempted here.
!.env.example
# Same blanket *.md rule, seventh instance: it only exempts specific
# root-level filenames, so anything under docs/ was silently swallowed --
# docs/demo-script.md existed on disk with a clean `git status` the whole
# time. Exempting the directory rather than one more filename, so future
# docs/ files don't repeat this.
!docs/
!docs/*.md
# Eighth instance of the same trap, found immediately: `docs/*.md` only
# matches files directly inside docs/, not a subdirectory -- docs/pitch-deck/deck.md
# was still silently swallowed. `**` crosses directory boundaries.
!docs/**/*.md
# docs/pitch-deck-plan.md is meta-planning for how the deck itself was
# designed (layout research, template choices), not part of the trading
# system's research story -- excluded even though the exception above
# would otherwise let it through. Never committed, so no `git rm --cached`
# needed for this one.
docs/pitch-deck-plan.md

# Runtime-generated bot artifacts that predate any rule matching their
# extension (output/audit/*.jsonl and output/data/*.csv were already
# covered; these were untracked only by luck, not by an explicit rule).
output/audit/*.log
output/audit/*.json

# Local-only admin-panel state (pipeline/execution/pause.py) -- never
# meant to sync anywhere, same as the audit log and data caches above.
output/state/
output/data/*.json
